markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Sort the AI Approaches

In Lesson 1, students move into the Intelligence Card Sort right after the warm-up, where they first wrote their own working definition of intelligence individually. 

Working in pairs, they group real behaviors, human, animal, and machine, based on what kind of intelligence each one shows. 

Before you facilitate that discussion, try a version of the sort yourself below and notice how quickly "AI" stops feeling like one single thing.

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
  <iframe
    src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/AIFY2/unit-1/ai-approaches-sort.html"
    width="100%"
    height="1150"
    frameborder="0"
    scrolling="no"
    title="Sort AI examples into Rule-Based Logic or Learns from Data"
    style="display:block; border-radius:10px;">
